title: Roguelike fighting
intro: Bump into a monster to hit it, turn by turn, and pick up potions to drink with the number keys. No code.
project: Empty | Slime Crawl

chapter: A hero who hits by walking | Bump Attack
create: Tilemap
rename: Level
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 11111111\n1......1\n1......1\n11111111
select: Main Camera
set: Transform.Position.X = 4
set: Transform.Position.Y = -2
look: 4, -2, 3.5
deselect
create: Grid Player
set: Transform.Position.X = 1.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1.5
add: Health
set: Health.Max = 5
set: Health.Current = 3
set: Health.InvincibleTime = 0
say: A small room and a grid player, a little hurt: three hit points of five.
add: BumpAttack
explain: component:BumpAttack | Bump Attack | A Bump Attack makes walking into a monster hit it instead of bumping into it.
explain: field:BumpAttack.Layers | Layers | It hurts things on the Enemy layer, a hit point at a time.
add: Inventory
set: Inventory.ItemUses = Potion: heal 2
explain: field:Inventory.ItemUses | Item Uses | And the inventory says what its items do. A potion heals two hit points. Bombs could spawn an explosion, and scrolls send a message.
explain: field:Inventory.NumberKeys | Number Keys | The number keys use them: one for the first item it holds that has a use.

chapter: A potion and a slime | Pickups and a monster that hits back
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Potion
set: Transform.Position.X = 2.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -2.5
set: Sprite.Size = 0.4, 0.4
set: Sprite.Tint = #E04060
add: BoxCollider
set: BoxCollider.IsTrigger = true
add: Pickup
set: Pickup.Item = Potion
say: A potion to pick up: its Pickup puts a Potion in the inventory of whoever steps on it.
deselect
create: Grid Enemy
set: Transform.Position.X = 6.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1.5
set: GridChase.Range = 0
set: GridChase.StopDistance = 0
click: remove:Attack
select: Hitbox
menu: Entity > Delete
select: Enemy
add: Health
set: Health.Max = 2
set: Health.Current = 2
set: Health.InvincibleTime = 0
add: BumpAttack
set: BumpAttack.Layers = Player
explain: component:BumpAttack | A monster's Bump Attack | The slime chases the player right into its cell, so with a Bump Attack on the Player layer, it hits the player too.
deselect
create: Turn Order
explain: menu:Entity | Gameplay, Turn Order | And a turn order: everything moves when the player moves.

chapter: Fight | Turn by turn
play
wait: 0.5
tap: Down
wait: 0.5
tap: Right
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Player.Inventory.Items = Potion
say: The player steps onto the potion and picks it up. Each step, the slime steps closer.
tap: D1
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Player.Health.Current = 5
explain: game | Drinking it | Pressing one drinks it, back to full health. Using it took a turn, so the slime came closer again.
tap: Up
wait: 0.6
expectvalue: Player.Health.Current = 4
say: The slime walks into the player and hits it.
tap: Right
wait: 0.6
expectvalue: Enemy.Health.Current = 1
expectvalue: Player.Health.Current = 3
explain: game | Bump to hit | The player walks into the slime, lunging and hitting it, and the slime hits back on its turn.
tap: Right
wait: 0.6
expectcount: Enemy = 0
say: One more hit and it's gone.
stop
say: That's roguelike fighting with no code: a Bump Attack for anything that steps on the grid, and items with uses for the number keys.
